  "rationale": "The advisor requested income generation on AAPL with low assignment risk in an IRA-eligible account. A covered call ladder against an existing long AAPL position is the most direct match: it generates premium income, the underlying long share position fully covers the short call obligation (no naked exposure permitted in IRAs), and the 30-delta short strike target keeps the probability of assignment below ~30% while maintaining attractive yield. We applied a 7-day earnings blackout window because AAPL has been a high-realized-vol earnings trade historically, and a 50% profit-take rule to compound gains. This is a Reg-BI rationale stub — the advisor must review suitability against the specific client's investment objectives, time horizon, liquidity needs, and risk tolerance before approving the deployment.\n\nAssignment risk is further mitigated via the 0.50-delta roll trigger and the pin-risk window of 2 DTE: if the short call drifts deep ITM near expiry, the strategy automatically proposes a roll-up-and-out before assignment can occur. The 25% account-notional cap on covered positions prevents concentration risk if AAPL appreciates rapidly."
